cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Jiggle in your research, please cite it as below, together with OpenMM.
title: 'Jiggle: a live molecular dynamics viewer'
abstract: Jiggle is a desktop application that runs OpenMM molecular dynamics simulations and renders
  the structure in real time rather than replaying a finished trajectory. It reports live RMSD, per-residue
  RMSF, potential energy, radius of gyration and receptor-binder interface distance. For two-body systems
  RMSD is decomposed four ways, including a binder RMSD computed after superposition on the receptor,
  which isolates pose drift from global motion and from the binder's own internal rearrangement.
